==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|bawlen}}, from {{etyl|non|en}} {{m|non|baula||to low}} and/or {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{m|la|baulō||bark|pos=verb}}, both from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*bau-||to roar}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*bau-||to bark}}, conflated with {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*bellaną}}, {{m|gem-pro|*ballijaną}}, {{m|gem-pro|*buljaną||to shout, low, roar}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*bʰel-||to sound, roar}}. Cognate with {{etyl|is|-}} {{m|is|baula||to moo, low}}, {{etyl|sv|-}} {{m|sv|böla||to bellow, low}}. More at {{l|en|bell}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|[bɔːɫ]|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/bɔl/|lang=en}}
* {{a|cot-caught}} {{IPA|/bɑl/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɔːl|lang=en}}
* {{homophones|lang=en|ball}}<!--perhaps not in all dialects but in Australian English and in New York City-->

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{label|en|intransitive}} To [[shout]] in a loud and [[intense]] manner.
# {{label|en|intransitive}} To [[wail]]; to give out a [[blare#Verb|blaring]] [[cry]].

